 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 519225,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Apply the 50-30-20 budget philosophy to David’s budget.",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>The 50-30-20 principle suggests spending 50 percent of your budget on necessary expenses (basic living requirements and debt services such as mortgage/rent, utilities, car, insurance, health care, groceries, gasoline, child care, and minimum debt payments), 30 percent of your budget for wants (restaurants, vacations, hobby costs), and 20 percent should be set aside (retirement funds, stocks, an emergency fund should have at least 3 months of income, other investments).</p>\n<p>Monthly income is $3,450.</p>\n<table class=\"unnumbered\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td valign=\"top\"></td>\n<td valign=\"top\">50% Needs</td>\n<td valign=\"top\">30% Wants</td>\n<td valign=\"top\">20% Set Aside</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td valign=\"top\">Goal</td>\n<td valign=\"top\">$1,725.00</td>\n<td valign=\"top\">$1,035.00</td>\n<td valign=\"top\">$690.00</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td valign=\"top\">Actual</td>\n<td valign=\"top\">Rent: $925.00<br>Car payment: $178.54<br>Car insurance: $129.49<br>Credit card: $117<br>Gas: $195.00<br>Food: $290.00<br>Total: $1,835.03</td>\n<td valign=\"top\">Amazon Prime: $21.99<br>Going out: $400.00<br>Internet: $49.99<br>Total: $471.98</td>\n<td valign=\"top\">Unused: $1,142.99</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "David should allocate $1,735 to necessary expenses, $1,035 to expenses that are wants, and $690 to savings and extra debt service."
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  }
 ],
